From the Holy Book of <1992Jul23.162406.241@thunder.mcrcim.mcgill.edu>
  as spake by mackenzi@McRCIM.McGill.EDU (Paul Mackenzie) :
>But, every time I pray now, I see that my god is angry with me!  I know that
>one shouldn't pray too often, but I waited over 100 turns and still he's angry.

A hundred turns is nothing to a deity.  They generally measure their
umbrage in thousands of turns.

>What did I do that made him angry, and how do I make him pleased?

Did you kill any peaceful creatures?  Sacrifice any human types?  Kill a
shopkeeper?

Alternatively, it might just be the gods being fickle.  I can't count
the number of times my god has been angry at me when I'd done nothing to
deserve it.

As for what to do... Spoiler?

Find an altar.  Sacrifice everything and its uncle on it.  Swear loudly
at your idiot deity every time s/he claims your sacrifice is
"inadequate" [this last step is not necessary, but it helps ;) ].  This
will take lots and lots of monsters, so settle yourself in for some hard
work.  Repeat this until "the gods seem mollified" or "you have a
feeling of reconciliation".  Until you have seen this message, _do_not_
pray for _any_ reason.  At best you'll have to sacrifice several more
monsters; at worst you'll get yourself blue-bolted out of existence.

Good luck.
